Let me write `crosschecks.py` carefully. Use yaml.compose to detect duplicates:

```python
import yaml
def dup_keys(path):
    node = yaml.compose(open(path))
    dups=[]
    def walk(n, path_):
        if isinstance(n, yaml.MappingNode):
            seen={}
            for k,v in n.value:
                key=k.value
                if key in seen: dups.append((path_,key,seen[key],k.start_mark.line+1,k.start_mark.column))
                else: seen[key]=k.start_mark.line+1
                walk(v, path_+'.'+key)
        elif isinstance(n, yaml.SequenceNode):
            for i,item in enumerate(n.value): walk(item, f'{path_}[{i}]')
    walk(node,'$')
    return dups
```

This gives all duplicates with first/last line numbers.

